<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-mirror-realm-build-spec-for-mirror-wright`>>

! The mirror realm: build spec for Mirror-Wright

Spec-Scout: Lares (Tasked Spirit), 2026-10-29. This seat was read-only.

''Trees''
* ''WT'' = the D3 lane worktree, `~/.lares-scratch/d3-glass/wt` &#64; `afa95922e`. The glass code lives here.
* ''M'' = the main tree, `~/Synthetic-Dream-Machine` &#64; `2d6864b26`. The custody code lives here.
* `TiddlyWiki5/` sits at `ea94ca840` (`5.5.0-prerelease`), and its `boot/` and `core/` bytes match in both trees.
* A cite with no tree mark reads WT for `packages/lararium-tw5` and `packages/lararium-web/src/glass`, and M for `packages/lararium-browser` and `packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts`. The two `main.ts` files differ by about 90 lines, so re-anchor before editing.

''Citation marks''
* Web claims carry their URL.
* ''UNVERIFIED'' marks a claim whose page this seat never opened, or opened without finding the claim on it.
* ''⚑'' marks a place where a ruling meets a platform fact and the two do not fit. Each one goes to the operator; none gets smoothed over here.

''Inputs read''
* the ruling memo (`project_dreamdom_mirror_ruling`: MIRROR DEFAULT, WIDTH, REALM, PAGE NEVER A VESSEL)
* Realm-Scout's `out.md`
* `d3-glass-lane.mem` (#/the-mirror-realm and #/owed)
* `dreamdom.mem` (#/the-layers, #/the-crossings host services, #/what-a-replacement-un-skips, #/conformance, #/open-rulings)
* `dreamdom-roadmap.mem` (D3, D4, D5)
* `sealed-store.mem` (#/keys, #/the-store, #/what-the-code-holds, #/owed)
* `stable-founding-road.mem` (#/rulings, and the sealed store's five steps at :396-421)
* `secure-context.mem` (#/two-key-classes, #/storage-that-vanishes, #/custody-leans)
* `session-unlock-2026.mem`
* `project_browser_key_custody`
* `train-s3-launch.mem`

---

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/0-the-order-at-a-glance`>>

!! 0. The order, at a glance

```
A1 page boot env ─ A2 startup set + savers ─ A3 syncadaptor census ─ A4 window claims + alert rail
      └─ A5 camera under $tw.rootWidget + hooks ─ A6 lar-root-services in browser mode (G3 doors) ─ A7 route door (#:safe burns)
B1 custody into the daemon worker ─ B2 signers into the worker; device key non-extractable in memory, sealed at rest
      └─ B3 no clear row under the mirror; `?holder` burns or is re-cut ─ B4 the clean-realm ask (ceremony)
C1 browser rest + holder seat (step 2 rows) ─ C2 sealed repos + face-checked hydration (step 3 rows) ─ C3 the plugin gate opens
D  goldens 1–13 at full · G6 walk incl. WebKit · G7 phone measures · D4 the Wiki Actor
```

''How the lanes depend on each other''
* ''A and B share no files, so they run in parallel.''
** A touches `lararium-tw5` and `lararium-web/src/glass`.
** B touches `lararium-browser` and the custody half of `main.ts`.
* ''C waits on B1 and B2.'' The content-key holder must live in the same worker as the opened tree key.
* ''C3 waits on A3 and C2.''
* ''D runs after A.'' D's WebKit and phone rows may start once A5 stands.

''How nothing stages "a now, b later"''
* A ships the mirror at full with the ''plugin gate closed'': core plus house plugins only. The gate reads a capability the vessel's port grant carries. It never reads a flag.
* C3 opens the gate. No slice ships an interim shape that a later slice has to undo.

---

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/a-the-page-mirror-boots-in-tw5-s-own-browser-mod`>>

!! A. The page mirror boots in TW5's own browser mode

!!! A0. What the code does today, and what changes

''The boot chain'' (WT): `main.ts:523` `standPageMirror` → `page-mirror.ts:28` → `glass/stand.ts:177` `bootGlass(width:"skinny",deferPaint:true)` → `glass/boot.ts:21` `openMirror` → `lararium-tw5/src/glass-mirror.ts:45` `TW5Engine.boot(core, preloads, MIRROR_TOKEN)` → `tw5-vm.ts:54` `prepareHostBootInstance` → `tw5-vm.ts:65` `bootWithHostBridge` → `instance.boot.boot()` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:568`).

| Today (WT) | Changes to |h
| `makeBrowserWorkerBootEnv` serves the page too: `preSeedTw={boot:{suppressBoot:true}, node:{}, browser:null}` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:302`), a `process` shim (`:306`, body `:167-175`), and a scoped `window` Proxy (`:195,226-247,346`) | A page env of its own (A1) |
| `configureIslandRuntime` runs on the page: nulls `node`/`browser` (`:397-398`), stubs the DOM store reader (`:401-402`) and decrypt (`:405`), sets `tasks` (`:408`), sends `utils.error` to the alert rail (`:424-431`) | Off the page path. Only the alert-rail `utils.error` lend survives, as its own function (A4) |
| The page branch lends `global`, `Buffer`, `process`, `setImmediate`, `clearImmediate` (`:453-473`) and releases them only at `releaseGlass()` (`tw5-vm.ts:40,63`) | Burns: no lends (A1) |
| `nextTick = queueMicrotask` (`:479`) | ''Kept.'' It is a `$tw` property, not a byte change, and keeps event batching the same as the island (Realm-Scout A2) |
| The camera mints its own root widget and swaps `tw.rootWidget` (`glass-camera.ts:33-34`), lends `browser`, `pageScroller` and `popup` (`:40-49`), refreshes directly on `change` (`:61-66`), and emits no hook | It parents under the boot-time `$tw.rootWidget` and emits TW5's hooks and actions (A5) |
| `lar-root-services` returns when `$tw.browser` is truthy (M `lararium-tw5/src/modules/lar-root-services.ts:94`; header `:37` says "a browser page that runs stock TW5 keeps stock's own listeners") | Binds in browser mode on the mirror; its guard reads a capability (A6) |
| No `disabledStartupModules`, no `$:/config/*` overrides, no hook emission and no safe-mode handling anywhere in lane source | A2, A5, A7 |
| The unload hold (`page-mirror.ts:32-35`, `beforeunload` + `preventDefault` while `pending()>0`) | Kept, now beside a TW5 `onbeforeunload` that A4 retires |
| The width probe, its five steps, one step-down and the crash records (`glass/stand.ts:24-28,41-200,58-62,84-91,96-106,122-127`) | Unchanged. A1's boot runs inside step L3 |
| `flag.ts` / `?glass=` / `{glass:true}` | Already absent from both trees |
| The route door | Unbuilt (lane kit G3 owed, `d3-glass-lane.mem:58`); A7 builds the part the mirror needs |

''One bug the walk found.'' Both conditions below hold today, in WT and M:
* `lar-root-services` binds only where `$tw.browser` is null.
* The camera swaps in a fresh root widget.

So even an island-mode `lar-root-services` listener would sit on a root the mirror's widgets never bubble to. A5 and A6 cure both together.

!!! A1. The page boot env: browser mode, with no forge and no lends

''Platform facts''
* `bootprefix.js:29-34`: `$tw.browser` comes from `typeof window/document`, unless `"browser" in $tw`. `$tw.node` comes from `typeof process === "object"`, unless `"node" in $tw`.
* `bootprefix.js:39-42` overwrites `$tw.boot.tasks` without condition.
* `boot.js:2777-2779`: autoboot runs only when `!suppressBoot`.
* `boot.js:862` passes `Buffer` only when `$tw.browser` is falsy. The browser module executor runs `Function("return "+code)` (`boot.js:617`). So in browser mode ''no `Buffer`, `global` or `process` name gets read.'' That is the cure Realm-Scout named (out.md A0).

''Build''
# Add `makePageBootEnv()` beside `makeBrowserWorkerBootEnv` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:288`):
#* `preSeedTw = {boot:{suppressBoot:true}, node:null}`. `node:null` states a measured fact and closes the bundler-`process` hazard (out.md :26). Do ''not'' pre-seed `browser`; let `bootprefix` detect it.
#* no `processArg`, no `fs`/`vm` shims, and the real `window` passed as the `window` parameter.
# `prepareHostBootInstance` page branch (`:453-485`): delete the lends (`:455-473`), the `release` hold (`:474`) and the `configureIslandRuntime` call. Keep `MIRROR_TOKEN` (`:447-451`) and `nextTick` (`:479`).
# `bootWithHostBridge` (`:529-575`): the page path lends no `require`. Browser-mode modules resolve through `$tw.modules.execute`.
# The `process` parameter of the loader's `new Function` (`:353-354`) gets `undefined` on the page path.

''Tests: red first, each with its CONTROL''
* `mirror-boots-browser-mode` (vitest-browser or Playwright, Chromium and Firefox)
** Red today: after `openMirror`, `$tw.browser` is a truthy object and `$tw.node === null`.
** Control: the island boot (`makeBrowserWorkerBootEnv` in a Worker) still reads `browser === null && node === null`.
* `mirror-leaves-no-lends`
** Red today: while the mirror stands, `'Buffer' in window`, `'global' in window`, `'process' in window`, `'setImmediate' in window` and `'clearImmediate' in window` all read `false`.
** Control: those same five names, taken as a snapshot before the mirror boots, match after.
* `mirror-process-hazard-closed`
** Red: define `globalThis.process = {}` before boot and expect `$tw.node === null`.
** Control: drop the `node:null` pre-seed in a test-only env and `$tw.node` reads `{}`. This proves the instrument can see the hazard.

!!! A2. Which startup modules stand, which stay out, and the saver path

''TW5's two mechanisms, both CID-neutral''
* `$tw.boot.disabledStartupModules`: defaulted at `boot.js:2579`, honoured at `boot.js:2692,2699`.
* The shadow-module skip: `defineShadowModules` skips a shadow module whose title an ordinary tiddler holds (`boot.js:1539-1543`). A later plugin's shadow overrides an earlier one.

''⚑ Why the house cannot simply out-register stock handlers.'' Root-widget listeners ''accumulate'':
* `Widget.prototype.addEventListener` pushes onto an array (`core/modules/widgets/widget.js:708-713`).
* `dispatchEvent` calls ''every'' handler (`:731-756`).

So a house `tm-http-request` handler beside stock `rootwidget`'s would run ''with'' it, not instead of it. Any stock module whose root handlers must stay out has to be disabled by name.

''The startup walk'' (`core/modules/startup/*.js`; platforms and ordering from each file)

| Module | Platforms · order | Disposition | Evidence |h
| `load-modules` | — | ''stands'': builds `$tw.rootWidget` over the real `document` (`load-modules.js:46-51`) | the camera parents under it (A5) |
| `info` | — · before startup | ''stands'' (`$:/info`; the adaptor keeps `$:/info/browser` local, `glass-port-adaptor.ts:37`) | — |
| `plugins` | — · before startup | ''stands'' | — |
| `startup` | — | ''stands'': UA, language, theme, keyboard manager on `document`, StartupActions incl. `/Browser`, popup, anim. Its tail builds the Syncer only if a `syncadaptor` module exists (`startup.js:103-116`; A3 keeps the count at zero) and builds `SaverHandler` ''unconditionally'' (`:118-122`; made inert below) | — |
| `confirm` | — | ''stands'' (the confirm road per tab, ruled 2026-10-16) | `dreamdom.mem` #/open-rulings |
| `eventbus` | browser · before windows | ''stands'': an in-page bus, no window claim | — |
| `story` | — · after startup | ''disabled by name'' and replaced by a house module `lar-story` (see the note after this table) | `story.js:36-110` |
| `rootwidget` | browser · after startup, before story | ''disabled by name''. Its kinds move to `lar-root-services` (A6) | `rootwidget.js:31,57,61-111` |
| `render` | browser · after story | ''disabled by name''. The camera takes its behaviour (A5) | `render.js:23-118` |
| `password` | browser | ''disabled by name'': the house seals | `password.js:19-34` |
| `favicon` | browser | ''disabled by name''. The page belongs to the surface, and the surface sets its own icon | `favicon.js:21-36` |
| `windows` | browser | ''disabled by name''. `tm-open-window` crosses as the `open-surface` door (D4, roadmap :119) | `windows.js:25-110` (`window.open` with its own widget tree; an unload task) |
| `browser-messaging` | browser | ''disabled by name''. `tm-load-plugin-library` and friends refuse by name on the alert rail | `browser-messaging.js:94-158` (iframes to a web2 library URL; `window.addEventListener("message")`) |

''Why `story` gets replaced rather than kept'' (`story.js`):
* It opens the default tiddlers (`:36-39`), which the mirror wants.
* It also does five things the mirror refuses:
** writes `location.hash` on every StoryList change (`:40-48`, `updateLocationHash` ~`:227-230`);
** adds a window `hashchange` listener (`:50-58`);
** binds `tm-browser-refresh` (a reload), `tm-print`, `tm-open-external-window`, `tm-permalink` and `tm-permaview` on the root (`:60-110`). Those bypass the door law, and they ''cannot be out-registered'' (the ⚑ above).
* Setting `$:/config/Navigation/UpdateAddressBar` to `no` stops only the first of the five.
* So `lar-story` keeps `openStartupTiddlers` and `tm-home` (story and history only). It answers the other four kinds through doors:
** `print` and `open-external` as `lar:service` kinds;
** `tm-browser-refresh` as a `route` reload under the unload hold;
** permalink and permaview as `route` writes the route door owns (A7).
* This is house code beside unchanged core bytes, not a patch. Its witness compares `lar-story`'s opening of `$:/DefaultTiddlers` to stock `story` over the same world.

''The saver path, by config and override (no core byte)''
* ''What happens with no cure:'' `SaverHandler` runs `initSavers` in browser mode (`saver-handler.js:26-27,122-140`), which ''constructs every saver''. `put.js`'s constructor fires OPTIONS (`put.js:49-51`) and HEAD (`:17-24,59`) at the page URL whenever `canSave` reads `http(s):` (`:126-128`). An empty `SaverFilter` does ''not'' stop the constructor (Realm-Scout §A3; TiddlyPWA shadows `put.js` for the same reason, https://codeberg.org/valpackett/tiddlypwa).
* The cure, shipped as tiddlers of the ''house plugin'' with a plugin priority above core:
*# One tiddler per saver title, all fifteen of them (`$:/core/modules/savers/{andtidwiki,custom,download,fsosaver,gitea,github,gitlab,manualdownload,msdownload,postmessage,put,tiddlyfox,tiddlyie,twedit,upload}.js`). Each carries ''no `module-type`'', so the core shadow gets overridden and nothing gets defined.
*# `$:/config/SaverFilter` with empty text. The dirty listener then counts nothing, `tc-dirty` never lands on `document.body`, and the unload task returns nothing (`saver-handler.js:30-91,115,203-208`).
*# `$:/config/AutoSave` set to `no` (`:116,159`).
* ''Why a plugin shadow and not ordinary preload tiddlers:'' an ordinary tiddler would appear in the person's wiki and fire a `change` event that the port adaptor posts as a write.
* ''UNVERIFIED in this fork:'' that a house-plugin shadow beats core's shadow for `defineShadowModules`. The red test below settles it. If it fails, ship the fifteen as ''ordinary'' preloads and add their titles to the adaptor's local-only set (`glass-port-adaptor.ts:37,72-74`).
* `tm-download-file` still lives on the inert `SaverHandler` (`:103`). The house wants download as a door, so `lar-root-services` binds the download door. ''⚑ Both handlers would then run.'' The stock one calls the `download` saver, which A2 removed, so it finds no saver and does nothing. The witness proves that.

''Tests''
* `mirror-boot-makes-no-request` (Playwright, a page served over `http://127.0.0.1`)
** Red today: zero OPTIONS or HEAD requests from boot to first paint.
** ''Control:'' a stock TW5 HTML of the same commit, served the same way, makes them.
* `mirror-disabled-set-holds`: after boot, `$tw.boot.disabledStartupModules` equals the named set, and `$tw.pageContainer` belongs to the camera. ''Control:'' a stock boot defines `$tw.titlePublisher` and the mirror leaves it undefined.
* `mirror-saver-handler-inert`: edit 10 tiddlers. `document.body.classList.contains("tc-dirty") === false` and `$tw.unloadTasks.every(t => !t({}))`. ''Control:'' with the house plugin's three tiddlers removed, `tc-dirty` lands.
* `mirror-no-root-double-handler`: `$tw.rootWidget.eventListeners["tm-http-request"]` holds exactly one handler, `lar-root-services`'s. Likewise `tm-modal`, `tm-notify`, `tm-print` and `tm-open-window`.

!!! A3. The syncadaptor refusal at mount

''Fact.'' A Syncer exists if any module of type `syncadaptor` exports `adaptorClass` (`startup.js:103-116`). It gets built inside `startup`, so a check made after boot is already too late. The census therefore runs ''before'' boot, over the mirror's preloads.

''Build''
* `censusPreloads(preloads)` lives in `lararium-tw5/src/glass-mirror.ts`, before `TW5Engine.boot` (`:45`).
* For every plugin tiddler it parses the plugin JSON and counts shadow tiddlers whose `module-type` reads `syncadaptor` or `saver`, keyed by plugin title.
* ''The ruling's words'' ("a person's syncadaptor plugin refused at mount by name"): the counted ''plugin'' leaves the mirror's preloads.
** An alert tiddler `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/plugin-syncadaptor/<plugin title>` lands on the ''island's'' rail through the port's alert road. The mirror has not stood yet, so the island raises it.
** `data-lar-mirror` names `refused-plugin:<count>` beside the width.
** ''The mirror then stands without that plugin.'' This reads the ruling as refusing the plugin, not the mirror. See Q-A1 for the other reading.
* ''Belt after boot:'' `$tw.syncer === undefined && $tw.syncadaptor === undefined`, else the mirror takes teardown with `syncer-stood`. That catches a plugin whose own startup module builds a Syncer.

''Tests''
* `mirror-refuses-syncadaptor-plugin-by-name`: preload a fixture plugin carrying a `module-type: syncadaptor` tiddler (the tiddlyweb adaptor's shape). The alert names that plugin, `$tw.syncer` stays undefined, and the mirror paints. ''Control:'' the same plugin with the tiddler's module-type changed to `library` loads, and no alert appears.
* `mirror-refuses-saver-plugin-by-name`: likewise for `module-type: saver`.

!!! A4. Every page-window claim browser mode still makes, each with its disposition

| Claim | Site | Disposition |h
| `window.onerror` | `boot.js:252-257` runs at blob eval when `tasks.trapErrors` (set at `bootprefix.js:39-42`, which overwrites any pre-seed) | ''Uninstalled.'' Snapshot `window.onerror` before eval and restore it right after eval. Also set `$tw.boot.tasks.trapErrors=false`. No core byte changes |
| Error forms on `document.body` | `$tw.utils.error` paints only when `$tw.browser && !$tw.node` (`boot.js:203-242`) | Re-lent: `$tw.utils.error` is assigned the alert-rail writer now inside `configureIslandRuntime` (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:424-431`), extracted as `lendAlertRailError(tw)`. Assign it right after eval and before `boot.boot` |
| `window.onbeforeunload` | `initStartup`, `boot.js:2524-2536` | ''Restored'' to its prior value after boot. With `windows` disabled and the savers inert, `$tw.unloadTasks` stays empty. The house hold (`page-mirror.ts:32-35`) stays the one leave guard |
| `PasswordPrompt` div | built in `boot.boot` (`boot.js:2765-2767`), appended at `:644-650` | ''Detached'' after boot (`$tw.passwordPrompt.promptWrapper.remove()`), and `$tw.passwordPrompt` gets replaced by a stub whose `createPrompt` raises `refused/password` on the alert rail. Neither `password` nor any `#encryptedStoreArea` ever summons it |
| `window.sjcl` | read at `boot.js:785` when `$tw.Crypto` is built, then kept at `$tw.sjcl` (`:801`) | ''Deleted'' from `window` after `boot.boot` returns. ''UNVERIFIED:'' that no core path re-reads `window.sjcl` after boot. A grep witness pins it |
| `window.$tw` | the house loader passes `exports`, so `bootprefix.js:123` and `boot.js:2787-2791` take the exports branch; the loader reads `$tw` off the lend (`tw5-host-bridge.ts:349-355`) | ''Kept'' while the mirror stands: people's plugins name `$tw` bare from inline handlers. Removed at unmount. A stock claim, documented |
| `document.title` | `render.js:27-42` | `render` is disabled. The camera renders `$:/core/wiki/title` on `$tw.fakeDocument`, as stock does, and hands the text to the ''route door'', which owns `document.title` (A7) |
| `<style>` in `document.head` | `render.js:44-59` | `render` is disabled. The stylesheet goes into the shadow root's `<style>` (`glass-camera.ts:9-13,57-60`) |
| The DOM store-area reader | `loadTiddlersBrowser`, `boot.js:1846-1866`, reads `#storeArea` and `script.tiddlywiki-tiddler-store` off the ''page'' document | ''Stock, inert by witness.'' The page carries none of those selectors. The witness asserts it. No stub, since the stub at `tw5-host-bridge.ts:402` belongs to the forge |
| `keydown` on `document` | `startup.js:84-90` (the keyboard manager) | ''Stock.'' Global shortcuts belong to the surface the mirror paints. The none floor's own key road stays separate |
| `#:safe` and `location.hash` reads | `boot.js:2396-2401` | A7 |

''Tests''
* `mirror-window-claims-dispositioned`: after boot, `window.onerror`, `window.onbeforeunload` and `'sjcl' in window` equal their pre-boot snapshot. `document.body` gains no child from the engine. `#storeArea` is absent. ''Control:'' a stock TW5 page of the same commit shows all four claims.
* `mirror-fault-reaches-alert-rail`: a fixture plugin throws in a startup module. An alert tiddler `boot-fault/N` lands, and no `.tc-error-form` appears in `document.body`. ''Control:'' the same plugin on stock TW5 paints the error form.

!!! A5. The camera under `$tw.rootWidget`, with TW5's hooks

`render.js` gives the behaviour the camera has to match:
* `th-page-refreshing`, then refresh, then `th-page-refreshed` (`:79-85`);
* the draft throttle off `$:/config/Drafts/TypingTimeout`, default 400 (`:23-24,88-113`);
* `$:/tags/StartupAction/PostRender` after the first render (`:118`);
* the `rootWidget.domNodes` and `children` fix-up (`:115-116`);
* `$tw.pageWidgetNode`, `$tw.pageContainer` and `$tw.styleWidgetNode`/`styleElement` set as globals that plugins read. `modal.js:245` reads `$tw.pageContainer`.

''Build'' (`glass-camera.ts`)
* Drop the minted root (`:33-34`) and the `browser`/`pageScroller`/`popup` lends (`:40-49`). `load-modules` built the real `$tw.rootWidget`, `startup` built `$tw.popup`, and A6 builds `$tw.pageScroller`.
* Render `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` with `parentWidget: $tw.rootWidget` into the shadow container.
* Set `$tw.pageWidgetNode`, `$tw.pageContainer = container`, `$tw.styleWidgetNode` and `$tw.styleElement = shadowStyle`.
* Run the `domNodes`/`children` fix-up, emit both hooks around every refresh, and apply the draft throttle as `render.js:88-113` does.
* Invoke `PostRender` once after first paint.
* ''No global now:'' the throttle's `setTimeout` paces paint and decides no truth (out.md C8). Write that line in the code.

''Tests''
* `camera-emits-page-refresh-hooks`: a hook counter tiddler module records `th-page-refreshing` and `th-page-refreshed` once per change batch. ''Control:'' stock TW5 records the same counts over the same edit script.
* `camera-runs-postrender-once`: a `$:/tags/StartupAction/PostRender` action writes a temp tiddler exactly once.
* `camera-draft-throttle`: typing into a draft refreshes the river at most once per `TypingTimeout`. ''Control:'' a non-draft edit refreshes at once.

!!! A6. `lar-root-services` binds in browser mode: the modal, notify and switcher root layer, and the G3 doors

''Ruled:'' modals and notifications paint in the surface root layer, `lar-root-services` owns the mirror's doors, and stock rootwidget would bypass the Web3-only http door.

''Why stock Modal and Notifier cannot simply re-route''
* They append to `document.body` (`modal.js:30-32,224`; `notifier.js:58`), outside the shadow root and its stylesheet.
* `rootwidget` would also install `$tw.httpClient`, and with it `tm-http-request` (`rootwidget.js:31-57`).

''Build'' (`M packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/lar-root-services.ts`, plus its `tiddlers/src/lar-root-services.js` twin and the plugin JSON)
# ''The guard'' (`:94`) reads a capability, never the host: install where `$tw.rootWidget` exists and the boot handed a surface capability (`$tw.larSurface`, set by the mirror's boot inputs or by the island's camera). The header (`:37`) gets rewritten.
# ''Mirror half:'' set `$tw.modal`, `$tw.notifier` and `$tw.pageScroller` to house objects that paint into the camera's ''root layer''.
#* The root layer is a `<div class="lar-root-layer">` inside the shadow root. A modal uses a shadow-root `<dialog>` opened with `showModal()`, so it reaches the ''top layer'' and inherits the shadow stylesheet (https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interactive-elements.html#dom-dialog-showmodal).
#* Each renders its template through widgets parented to `$tw.rootWidget`, as `modal.js` does.
#* `tm-modal`, `tm-show-switcher` and `tm-notify` bind here. `tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-focus-selector` and `tm-scroll` bind as `rootwidget.js:81-109` binds them, as pure wiki logic.
# ''Door half'', as the island's door law already reads (`dreamdom.mem` #/the-crossings, host services):
#* ''Through `lar:service`:'' clipboard, download (`tm-download-file`), `open-surface` (`tm-open-window`), `print`, `open-external`, `fullscreen` and `route`.
#* ''Refused by name:'' `http-request`, until D15 builds it.
#* A kind outside the surface's manifest raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/<kind>` (`:107`).

''Tests''
* `mirror-modal-paints-in-root-layer`: `tm-modal` puts a `dialog[open]` inside the shadow root, and `document.body` gains nothing. ''Control:'' the island camera's `tm-modal` still writes the frame hint.
* `mirror-http-request-refused-by-name`: `tm-http-request` makes no network request, and the alert reads `refused/http-request`. ''Control:'' stock TW5 fires the request.
* `mirror-services-doors`: covers golden 12 at full, with copy and download `applied` and print refused.

!!! A7. The route door owns the URL, and `#:safe` burns

''Facts''
* `initStartup` reads `location.hash` before any config can speak. `#:safe` sets `$tw.safeMode` (`boot.js:2396-2401`), and that changes the Wiki's indexers and plugin registration (`:2517,2556,2559`).
* `getLocationHash` feeds `$tw.locationHash`.
* `#:safe` is the only `:safe` site in `boot/` and `core/`.

''Cure, with no patch''
# The route door stands before any mirror boot. It reads the full URL into its own route state and calls `history.replaceState` to drop any fragment. So `initStartup` always reads an empty hash.
# The route door adds the ''first'' `hashchange` listener on `window` and calls `stopImmediatePropagation()`. With `story` disabled (A2), no TW5 listener stands anyway, and this holds the line against a person's plugin.
# `#:safe` burns. A safe mode, if wanted, rides a face intent (ruled).
# `lar-story`'s permalink and permaview write through `route`.

''Tests''
* `route-door-burns-safe-hash`: open `…/#:safe`. `$tw.safeMode` stays falsy and the URL keeps no fragment. ''Control:'' a stock TW5 page at `#:safe` reads `safeMode === true`.
* `route-door-owns-hashchange`: setting `location.hash = "#Foo"` opens nothing in the story and lands in the route state. ''Control:'' stock TW5 opens `Foo`.
* `mirror-story-never-writes-hash`: navigating ten tiddlers leaves `location.hash` empty.

