!! D. The owed DreamDOM rows the Fable lane carries next

| Row | Fits after | What changes because of A to C |h
| ''Goldens 1–13 at full against stock TW5'' (roadmap D3 "Proves"; `dreamdom.mem` #/conformance) | A complete (A1–A9) | The oracle is a stock TW5 HTML of `ea94ca840` in Playwright. The mirror is now stock in browser mode (no forge), so most goldens should read identical writes and messages. Expected deliberate diffs: golden 12 (doors: print refused, download as a door), golden 7 (global shortcuts on the shadow surface), and permalink/route behaviour. Each diff records a named refusal per `page-controls#/refusals`, never a silent skip. Golden 14 waits on D4 |
| ''G3 doors'' | A6 and A7 | A6 builds modal, notify, switcher, clipboard, download, open-surface, print and fullscreen. A7 builds route. `http-request` stays refused until ''D15'' (door law, a per-face allowlist, private ranges refused, the response as a sensed snapshot), with goldens on a recorded fixture |
| ''G6 walk on WebKit'' | A8 | WebKit refuses to launch on this WSL host for want of two system libraries (`d3-glass-lane.mem:58`). Run it in the official Playwright Docker image (`mcr.microsoft.com/playwright`, version-matched to the repo's <code>&#64;playwright/test</code>), or on a Mac for real Safari. ''Re-anchor the image tag before use; UNVERIFIED here.'' The walk adds A8's shadow-root FramedEngine check. Safari's randomized Ed25519 signatures do not touch this walk, but they do touch any WebKit run of B2 |
| ''G7 phone measures'' | A5 (paint path final) and B1 (worker owns custody) | Re-run the shipped-setup table: process RSS against the +25% / 150 MiB gate, first paint, keystroke p95, peer write, echo, hot swap. ''Browser mode changes the inputs'' (stock `startup` UI managers, no `render`), so the WSL figures re-measure too. Phones: iOS 26 Safari, ''as a tab and as a Home Screen app'' (two storage regimes, `secure-context.mem` #/storage-that-vanishes), and Android Chrome, through `tools/capability-probe/`. Add the B4 clean-realm reload cost (the time from the lock to a re-asked first paint) |
| ''D4 the Wiki Actor'' | C3 (custody and seal in the worker), and the session contract's surface-open | The actor's attachments `{cursor, subscriptions, width, actorKey, localFilter, cameraMount}` now include the mirror's grant fields (`sealedRest`, width). The in-memory txId ledger of a G4 hand-off (`d3-glass-lane.mem` #/owed) moves into the actor's per-port attachments, resting ''sealed'' in the worker (C2a). `tm-open-window` → `open-surface` (A2 disables `windows`). Golden 14 and the seven D4 witnesses (roadmap D4 "Proves") follow |

